---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="WorshipMetrics Privacy Policy, including SMS/mobile information and AI voice data practices."
  canonical="/privacy"
>
  <section class="bg-white px-6 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-10">Last updated: July 22, 2026</p>
      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
          This Privacy Policy describes how WorshipMetrics collects, uses, and protects your
          information when you use our services.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              We collect information you provide directly (name, email, phone number, church
              details), information generated by your use of our services (attendance records,
              member data you enter), and technical information (device type, browser, usage
              patterns) to provide and improve our services.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              We use your information to provide the WorshipMetrics service, send transactional
              emails and text messages you have opted in to receive, improve the platform, and
              communicate with you about your account. We do not sell your data to third parties.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div id="sms">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">3. SMS/Text Messaging and Mobile Information</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                If you opt in to receive text messages from WorshipMetrics, we collect and use your
                mobile phone number solely to deliver the messages you have consented to receive,
                such as account notifications, AV system alerts, and church communications sent
                through the platform.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong class="text-slate-900">
                  No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for
                  marketing or promotional purposes. Text messaging originator opt-in data and
                  consent will not be shared with any third parties, excluding aggregators and
                  providers of the text message services necessary to deliver messages.
                </strong>
              </p>
              <p>
                Message frequency varies based on your notification settings and your church's
                activity. Message and data rates may apply. You can opt out at any time by replying
                STOP, and get assistance by replying HELP or emailing{" "}
                <a
                  href="mailto:support@worshipmetrics.com"
                  class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-700 underline"
                >
                  support@worshipmetrics.com
                </a>. See our{" "}
                <a href="/terms#messaging" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-700 underline">
                  SMS/Text Messaging Terms
                </a>{" "}
                for full details.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="ai-voice">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">4. AI Voice and Call Data</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Some calls and messages may be generated or assisted by artificial intelligence,
              including our AI assistant, Luminos. Where permitted by law and with notice, calls may
              be recorded or transcribed for quality, support, and service improvement. Recordings
              and transcripts are handled under the same protections as the rest of your data, are
              not sold, and are not shared with third parties for marketing or promotional purposes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">5. Data Retention</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Free Forever plan data is retained for 90 days of inactivity. Paid plan data is retained for
              the duration of your subscription plus 30 days after cancellation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">6. Security</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              We use industry-standard encryption and security practices. Your church and member
              data is stored securely and access is controlled through role-based permissions.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">7. Contact</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Questions about this policy? Email{" "}
              <a href="mailto:paul@worshipmetrics.com" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-700 underline">
                paul@worshipmetrics.com
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
